## What it does

`apps/web` is the reader site. [Foldkit](/lore/a-browser-send-follows-one-path) renders and hydrates most routes.
The HTML pages at `/news`, `/news/latest`, and `/directory` render and hydrate their content with [Effect UI](https://ui.effect.website/article.md) inside the reader shell.
Foldkit is a UI framework on [Effect](/lore/effect-basics): a Model, Messages, an `update` function, and a pure view.

Server rendering means the Worker builds the page HTML for each request.
Prerendering means the build writes page HTML to files before deployment.
Hydration means the browser program adopts HTML that the server rendered and continues from it.

One `vite build` makes three outputs:

- The browser bundle that hydrates each page.
- The server `fetch` function that Foldkit generates from `src/entry.server.ts`.
- One HTML file for each path in the server entry's `prerenderPaths` export.

`Cloudflare.Website.Foldkit` deploys the outputs as one Worker. A request for a prerendered page gets the file. Any other request goes to the server `fetch` function. It renders the page, an error page, or a 404 with its real status.

[Tube video pages](/systems/tube) use this reader to prerender transcript summaries and load a video player only after the reader presses play.

The server forwards `/rpc` to the private RpcBackend Worker. Browser Commands call capabilities through that path.

## Effect UI

[Effect UI](/glossary#e) continues the work of Foldkit 0.x. The [announcement](https://ui.effect.website/article.md) says the future full-stack Foldkit will use Effect UI as its frontend.

Effect UI is usable today. As of 26 November 2026, its packages install from [commit snapshots on pkg.pr.new](https://pkg.pr.new/~/Effect-TS/ui), not npm. Take every Effect UI package from the same commit, as the [README](https://github.com/Effect-TS/ui/blob/e2cb60ec65f2f2bd37813c5c5dc5378c42b03c85/README.md#snapshots) says. `@effect/ui` runs on Effect 4.1.4, the version rat-stack pins: its [peer range](https://github.com/Effect-TS/ui/blob/e2cb60ec65f2f2bd37813c5c5dc5378c42b03c85/packages/ui/package.json) is `^4.1.4`.

The framework covers components, routing, server rendering, hydration, and test harnesses ([README](https://github.com/Effect-TS/ui/blob/e2cb60ec65f2f2bd37813c5c5dc5378c42b03c85/README.md#packages)). The README marks the packages experimental. There is no upgrade guide from Foldkit 0.x yet; the authors say the move “will be an upgrade, not a rewrite.” Foldkit 0.x gets critical bug fixes until Effect UI ships with an upgrade guide.

A new project can start on Effect UI from a pinned snapshot. Rat-stack itself stays on [Foldkit 0.170.0](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/b633555b638cd44f4dfe9d16aa7b9d4b45f9a122/AGENTS.md#stack-contract) until Effect UI is on npm and has an upgrade guide, because its pins are exact npm versions.

## The standard

- `vite.config.ts` turns on rendering with one `foldkit({ ssr })` call. It uses the default `dist/client` and `dist/server` directories.
- The server entry exports `renderPage`, `renderDocument`, and `prerenderPaths`.
- Every finite public page is prerendered. Pages that depend on the request render on the server.
- Readable content and links work before browser JavaScript runs.
- A missing page returns a real 404. It never falls back to the home page.
- Production builds contain no development modules, devtools code, or test people.
- Pages follow the reader's light or dark system setting from the first paint. `apps/site/src/rat.css` declares `color-scheme: light dark` and holds every colour token, with the dark values under `prefers-color-scheme: dark`. No script picks the theme. Code blocks render Catppuccin Latte in light mode and Mocha in dark mode.

## How to check

- Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/web build`. Read `apps/web/dist/server/foldkit.build.json`. It names `fetch.js` as the server entry and lists the prerendered paths.
- Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/web test` for page parity and the production-bundle exclusion test.
- Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/site test -- contrast`. It reads the served stylesheet and checks every text and accent token pair against WCAG AA in both palettes. It also checks the shipped code colours.
- Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/infra test`. The Website build test builds through [Alchemy](/skills/learn-alchemy), reads prerendered pages, and serves them, `/rpc`, and a 404 from the server bundle in workerd.
- On a preview, request a prerendered page and an unknown path with `curl`. The page returns complete HTML with `X-Preview-Commit`. The unknown path returns 404.
